  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1232 PM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nSubtropical Ridging will remain in place over the western\nPanhandle and northeastern New Mexico Monday-Friday, resulting in\nincreasingly hot conditions. Humidity should mix out a bit more\neach afternoon, with a stretch of triple digit heat expected for\nmost locations Tuesday-Friday. By next weekend, ridging starts to\nslide west into the Four Corners, which could open the door for\nnortherly flow and some low end rain chances. For now, with it\nbeing nearly a week away, have opted for a mainly dry forecast in\nthe long term.",
